From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: glacier <hyouga.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:37:18 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] A world and its chunks load without throwing to find things
 out

Two NumberFormatExceptions for each boolean game rule, each time a world was
made and again as its rules were read; an EOFException inside Gson for every
empty line of every sign; a NullPointerException for every head without an id
and a NumberFormatException for every empty flower pot: about 5,400 in one
recording of matches starting. The answers are the same. A scoreboard with no
objective for a criterion answers with the shared empty list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/GameProfileSerializer.java b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/GameProfileSerializer.java
index 350923a654cfafa59292f41b4ee916d98880f27c..8a96ca02cbfaf77771e9b574f89cbce661119d75 100644
--- a/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/GameProfileSerializer.java
+++ b/src/main/java/net/minecraft/server/GameProfileSerializer.java
@@ -24,6 +24,9 @@ public final class GameProfileSerializer {
         } else {
             UUID uuid;
 
+            if (s1 == null || s1.isEmpty()) { // Athena - a head with a name only: no exception to find that out
+                uuid = null;
+            } else
             try {
                 uuid = UUID.fromString(s1);
             } catch (Throwable throwable) {
